                <pb facs="0864" n="848" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg848"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/3–1849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Burdett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-18T08:00:00+02:00">March 18, 1949—8
                            a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                </p>
                <p>233. Palun 88. For Acheson from Ethridge. Technical study entitled “Arab refugee
                    problem” handed me yesterday by Israeli Government largely repeats Sharett’s
                    statement in previous conversations. Study begins with denial of responsibility,
                    minimizes dislocation and in brief can be summed up in one sentence “when the
                    whole matter comes up for discussion in the context of general peace talks the
                    Israeli Government will consider whether conditions are stable enough for a
                    certain number to come back without creating a security problem”. Study
                    emphasizes Israeli viewpoint that resettlement in Arab states is main solution
                    and not repatriation and continues with estimate of abilities of Arab states to
                    absorb them.</p>
                <p>Pouching text.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Baghdad 17, Damascus 14, Cairo 17, Jidda 8, Amman 18.
                    [Ethridge.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Burdett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
